{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "ASV1901",
  "book_code": "SNG",
  "chapter": 1,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "SNG.1.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:SNG.1.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The Song of songs, which is Solomon’s.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.1.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:SNG.1.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let him kiss me with the kisses of his mouth;\nFor thy love is better than wine.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.1.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:SNG.1.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thine oils have a goodly fragrance;\nThy name is ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "as",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " oil poured forth;\nTherefore do the virgins love thee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.1.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:SNG.1.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Draw me; we will run after thee:\nThe king hath brought me into his chambers;\nWe will be glad and rejoice in thee;\nWe will make mention of thy love more than of wine:Rightly do they love thee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.1.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:SNG.1.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I am black, but comely,\nO ye daughters of Jerusalem,\nAs the tents of Kedar,\nAs the curtains of Solomon.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.1.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:SNG.1.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Look not upon me, because I am swarthy,\nBecause the sun hath scorched me.\nMy mother’s sons were incensed against me;\nThey made me keeper of the vineyards;",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "But",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " mine own vineyard have I not kept.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.1.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:SNG.1.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Tell me, O thou whom my soul loveth,\nWhere thou feedest ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "thy flock",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ",\nWhere thou makest ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to rest at noon:\nFor why should I be as one that is veiled\nBeside the flocks of thy companions?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.1.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:SNG.1.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If thou know not, O thou fairest among women,\nGo thy way forth by the footsteps of the flock,\nAnd feed thy kids beside the shepherds’ tents.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.1.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:SNG.1.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I have compared thee, O my love,To a steed in Pharaoh’s chariots.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.1.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:SNG.1.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thy cheeks are comely with plaits ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "of hair",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ",\nThy neck with strings of jewels.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.1.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:SNG.1.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "We will make thee plaits of gold\nWith studs of silver.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.1.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:SNG.1.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "While the king sat at his table,\nMy spikenard sent forth its fragrance.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.1.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:SNG.1.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "My beloved is unto me ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "as",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a bundle of myrrh,\nThat lieth betwixt my breasts.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.1.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:SNG.1.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "My beloved is unto me ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "as",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a cluster of henna-flowers\nIn the vineyards of En-gedi.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.1.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:SNG.1.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Behold, thou art fair, my love;\nBehold thou art fair;Thine eyes are ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "as",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " doves.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.1.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:SNG.1.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Behold, thou art fair, my beloved, yea, pleasant:\nAlso our couch is green.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.1.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:SNG.1.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The beams of our house are cedars,",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "And",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " our rafters are firs.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    }
  ]
}
